      say: `Lab 2 moves to a test tenant with fictional people, never production, and it still only reads. You grant the same two read permissions, write a small set of inputs for the test accounts, and run it. Then come two checks the chapter couldn't settle from the documentation: what the license read actually shows in a GCC tenant, including whether a trial appears, and which identities the Conditional Access screen really lets you pick. Record both, discard the draft policy, and back everything out.`,
      detail: `Use a test tenant in the worldwide or GCC cloud, never production, with fictional people, and the Lab 2 runs of Chapters 01 and 02 (out/inventory-test, out/ownership-test). The run only reads. 1 Grant the two application permissions from Lab 1, step 2, to the app Chapter 01's Lab 2 registered, with admin consent. Nothing else. 2 Write the inputs for the test accounts: a workloads.csv row and a dispositions.csv row for each, a waves.csv with one wave and a rollback owner who is an enabled test user, program-dates.json, and a workload-id-premium.json listing one single-tenant test app as Tier 1. 3 Run it, signed in as in Chapter 01: Connect-MgGraph -Environment Global -TenantId <tenant-id> -ClientId <app-id> -CertificateThumbprint <thumbprint>; ./Invoke-NpiMatrix.ps1 -Cloud gcc -RegisterRun out/inventory-test -OwnershipRun out/ownership-test -InputPath <inputs> -OutputPath out/matrix-test. 4 Check the license read: record what workload-id-premium.json's tenant section shows: the skuPartNumber and service plans of any Workload ID subscription, or none, and whether a trial appears (research gaps, row 28). 5 Check eligibility against the admin center: on Conditional Access, start a new policy, choose Workload identities, and confirm the single-tenant test app can be selected and a managed identity can't; check whether a legacy service principal is offered (row 27). Discard the draft. 6 Back it out: remove the two permissions, and delete out/matrix-test: it lists the accounts kept on Kerberos and who owns them.`,
